The current development-approved pattern is file-based model-registry artifacts. Database-backed model storage is not required before diagnostic work continues, but the schema should anticipate eventual promotion if approved models become part of production recommendation flows.[4] [5]

## 9. Source Governance and Data Dependencies

The application must distinguish **external source evidence**, **internal workpapers**, **application-facing seed tables**, **runtime data retrieved through APIs**, **regression fixtures**, **development diagnostics**, and **model-registry artifacts**. Workpapers and external guidance can support seed values, but executable artifacts must be controlled, versioned, and status-labeled. This distinction is essential for auditability and maintenance.[8]

| Source Class | Examples | V4 Treatment |
|---|---|---|
| Runtime API | ATTOM property data, Census/ACS, HUD, FHFA, market sources | Accessed through adapters; log source status and response provenance |
| Static public dataset | Downloaded CSVs, geographic tables, market reference data | Register in Static Data Source Register V2; record download date and refresh expectation |
| Regression fixture | Corrected Greenville comparable-sales CSV | Retain as known-good local fixture for pipeline validation; do not treat as production calibration by itself |
| Static workpaper | Home Improvement Project Duration Estimates, Home Improvement Project Sequencing Analysis | Supporting evidence only; not directly executable |
| Seed table | Duration/lead-time rules, dependency rules, anomaly rules, DOM impact table | Application-facing executable input; versioned and review-status controlled |
| Development diagnostic | Greenville smoke regression diagnostics JSON | Engineering/model-review evidence only; not product-consumable |
| Model-registry artifact | `model_registry/greenville_sc/hedonic_ppsf_v0_1.json` | Product artifact pattern; only consumable when structurally valid, approved, and `approved_for_recommendations: true` |
| Governance artifact | Decisions Logs V10/V11/V12, Open Questions Log | Controls technical direction and unresolved blockers |

The full Static Data Source Register V2 should incorporate addendum rows for duration estimates, sequencing analysis, Angi/HomeAdvisor guidance, Decisions Log V11, duration/lead-time seed table, and regression-governance artifacts where relevant. Each source row should include a canonical source name, artifact path or URL, access date, source scope, confidence label, review status, and decision reference.[8]

